From: Codex M4 Android17 SELinux compatibility
Subject: [PATCH] Adapt BZI6 SELinux policy to Hybrid Vendor VNDK33

Reason: BZI6 Android17's VNDK33 mapping expands 16 public aliases absent from
our retained hybrid vendor, changes the telephony property label, and adds a
system_ext proc label that conflicts with a stale vendor genfscon. The previous
unmodified staged policy failed at system_ext mapping 33.0.cil:359; the exact
adapter now yields a clean staged secilc compile.
Files: add a narrowly scoped BZI6 policy adapter and call it after embedded
SELinux compatibility rules in the existing Exynos9810 finalization module.
Verification: helper self-test, wrong-VNDK reject, idempotent actual-workdir
transformation, staged fork SELinux verifier PASS, bash syntax, and full pinned
fork-series replay. No live policy load or device partition write.
Rollback: remove this patch from patches/fork/series and restore the previous
fork worktree; the original M2/AZH4 policy path is unchanged.

diff --git a/unica/patches/exynos9810_device_stack/exynos9810_finalization/customize.sh b/unica/patches/exynos9810_device_stack/exynos9810_finalization/customize.sh
